course: dictionary
lesson: 15766
title: Trying: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «Mia is trying hard to tie her shoelace.» Trying here means making an effort to do something.
explain: «Dad is trying the new cheese to see if he likes it.» Now trying means testing something, so you find out whether you like it. Ask yourself: is the writer working at something, or testing something?
explain: «It was a trying day: the bus broke down, it rained, and we lost our bags.» Here trying is an adjective. It describes the day, and the clues show it was annoying and hard to put up with. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Trying is the -ing form of the verb try, and it can also be an adjective.
fact: «Trying» can mean making an effort: «She is trying to finish her sums before lunch.»
fact: «Trying» can mean testing something to see if it works or if you like it: «We are trying a new experiment.»
fact: As an adjective, «trying» means annoying and hard to put up with: «a trying day».
fact: Phrases with trying: trying on clothes means putting them on to check the fit; trying out means testing something; keep trying means do not give up.
exercise: «Keep trying, you are nearly there.» What does trying mean here? | Stopping | *Making an effort | Annoying and hard to put up with | Testing a new food
exercise: «We are trying a new flavour of ice cream.» What does trying mean here? | Forgetting something | Being very annoying | *Testing to see if we like it | Shouting loudly
exercise: «It was a trying day, with rain, a flat tyre and a lost bag.» What does trying suggest? | Very quiet | Quick and easy | *Annoying and hard to put up with | Fun and exciting
test: Our goal is 20 points and we have 12 so far. «We keep trying to reach our goal.» How many more points are we trying to get? | 20 | *8 | 32 | 12
test: «Ravi got a strange result, so he is trying the experiment again to check it.» What is Ravi doing? | *Checking the result by repeating the experiment | Making a louder noise | Eating his lunch | Throwing the experiment away
exam: «Ana found the queue a trying wait.» What does trying mean here? | Making an effort to win | Testing a new recipe | *Annoying and hard to put up with | Calm and peaceful
